Subject: Modeling Algorithms - BOPAlgo_PaveFiller::MakeBlocks leaves out a section edge built without a 3D curve
Upstream: an issue is drafted for Open-Cascade-SAS/OCCT, not yet posted; its URL goes here once it is.
Applies to: OCCT V7_9_3.
Why: a crash Silico can't work around. A cone of radius 5 to 0 and height 5, and a level rod of
     radius 1 touching its side at one point (half height, 300 degrees round), fused, cut, or
     commoned: the face-face intersection gives a section curve whose pave block's ends meet at
     one vertex (a B-spline 3.5e-6 long, never more than 2.0e-7 from its start, against a
     tolerance of 1.5e-7: noise at a true point contact), BRepLib_MakeEdge marks it
     degenerated, BOPTools_AlgoTools::MakeEdge so builds it without a 3D curve, and
     BOPTools_AlgoTools::MakePCurve wraps that null curve in a Geom_TrimmedCurve, which
     dereferences it (SIGSEGV). It's reached on Silico's deterministic build's floating-point
     path; FreeCAD 1.1.3's conda-forge OCCT 7.9.3 doesn't reach it from the same B-reps, and
     builds each: the fuse both solids, 193.731546971 (125*pi/3 + 20*pi), the cut the cone whole,
     130.8996939, the common nothing. A section with no curve is no section: it's left out, as a
     pave block with no valid range is, so the operation goes on as FreeCAD's does.
Moves: nothing expected (no stress, oracle, or fingerprint digest; a boolean that reaches it
     crashed before).
Drop when: an OCCT release checks the section edge's 3D curve before MakePCurve (read MakeBlocks
     and MakePCurve; OCCT master doesn't, 2026-10-26), and boolean_degenerate_section.rs still
     passes without the patch. The test alone isn't enough: the crash depends on the exact
     floating-point path, so a release or recipe that moves the intersection's numbers can pass
     it with the dereference still there.

--- a/src/BOPAlgo/BOPAlgo_PaveFiller_6.cxx
+++ b/src/BOPAlgo/BOPAlgo_PaveFiller_6.cxx
@@ -999,6 +999,16 @@
         //
         // Make Edge
         BOPTools_AlgoTools::MakeEdge(aIC, aV1, aT1, aV2, aT2, aTolR3D, aES);
+        // A section edge built without a 3D curve (degenerated: faces that touch at a point,
+        // its ends on one vertex) is no section, and MakePCurve would dereference its null
+        // curve: it's left out, as a block with no valid range is.
+        {
+          Standard_Real aTF, aTL;
+          if (BRep_Tool::Curve(aES, aTF, aTL).IsNull())
+          {
+            continue;
+          }
+        }
         // Make p-curves
         BOPTools_AlgoTools::MakePCurve(aES,
                                        aF1,
